---
title: 'Financial Charts - Volume Profile'
enterprise: true
---

A Volume Profile shows the volume traded at each price level as horizontal bars against the price axis. It can be shown within a Financial Chart, or on its own as a Volume Profile Chart.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Volume Profile" name="volume-profile" type="generated" /%}

## Data

Volume Profile data has one row per price level, holding the price and the volume bought and sold at that price:

```js format="snippet"
{
    data: [
        { price: 135, upVolume: 3873690, downVolume: 3499965 },
        { price: 137.5, upVolume: 15861342, downVolume: 13138794 },
        { price: 140, upVolume: 19126307, downVolume: 25942209 },
    ],
    priceKey: 'price', // default
    upKey: 'upVolume',
    downKey: 'downVolume',
}
```

## Financial Chart

Set `volumeProfile` on a Financial Chart to show a Volume Profile alongside the price data, as in the example at the top of this page. It takes its own `data`, separate from the chart's `data`.

```js format="snippet"
{
    data: prices,
    volumeProfile: {
        data: profile,
        upKey: 'upVolume',
        downKey: 'downVolume',
    },
}
```

Hovering the chart shows the price level under the pointer in the [status bar](./financial-charts-configuration/#chart-features), after the price data values: its price range, up volume, down volume and total volume.

## Volume Profile Chart

Use a Volume Profile Chart to show a Volume Profile on its own, against a price axis.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Volume Profile Chart" name="volume-profile-chart" type="generated" /%}

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

```js
const options = {
    data: getVolumeProfile(),
    upKey: 'upVolume',
    downKey: 'downVolume',
};

AgCharts.createVolumeProfileChart(options);
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("react") %}

```jsx format="reactHooks"
const [options, setOptions] = useState({
    data: getVolumeProfile(),
    upKey: 'upVolume',
    downKey: 'downVolume',
});

return <AgVolumeProfileChart options={options} />;
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}

```ts
@Component({
    selector: 'app-root',
    standalone: true,
    imports: [AgVolumeProfileChart],
    template: `<ag-volume-profile-chart [options]="options"></ag-volume-profile-chart>`,
})
export class AppComponent {
    public options: AgVolumeProfileChartOptions;
    constructor() {
        this.options = {
            data: getVolumeProfile(),
            upKey: 'upVolume',
            downKey: 'downVolume',
        };
    }
}
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}

```js format="snippet"
template: `<ag-volume-profile-chart :options="options"/>`,
components: {
    'ag-volume-profile-chart': AgVolumeProfileChart,
},
data() {
    return {
        options: {
            data: getVolumeProfile(),
            upKey: 'upVolume',
            downKey: 'downVolume',
        },
    };
}
```

{% /if %}

Hovering a price level shows a tooltip.

### Selecting Price Levels

Set `selection.enabled` to let users select price levels. Selection is only available in a Volume Profile Chart.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Selecting Price Levels" name="selection" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    selection: {
        enabled: true,
        enableDrag: true,
    },
}
```

In this example:

- Click a price level to select it, or drag across the chart to select every level the rectangle touches.
- Use the Click Mode buttons to switch `selection.clickMode` between `'single'` and `'multiple'`.
- See [Selection](./selection/) for styling and the Selection API, and [Events](./events/#selectionchange) to respond to selection changes.

## Tick Size

Set `tickSize` to the price increment of the instrument to fix the height of each price level. Without it, each level is as high as the smallest gap between prices in the data.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Tick Size" name="tick-size" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    tickSize: 2.5,
}
```

In this example:

- Each price is rounded to the nearest multiple of `tickSize`, and the volumes of prices that round to the same level are added together.
- Every level between the lowest and highest price is shown, so the levels stay evenly spaced. Levels with no data are left empty.
- With the Irregular data and Tick Size Auto, the smallest gap between prices sets the level height, giving thin, uneven bars. Choose a Tick Size to group them into regular levels.
- A larger `tickSize` merges more prices into each level, giving fewer, taller bars.

## Total Segment

Set `totalSegment.enabled` to show each price level's total volume in a column between the price axis and the bars.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Total Segment" name="total-segment" type="generated" /%}

In a Volume Profile Chart, `totalSegment` is a top-level option. In a Financial Chart, set it on `volumeProfile`:

```js format="snippet"
{
    volumeProfile: {
        data: profile,
        upKey: 'upVolume',
        downKey: 'downVolume',
        totalSegment: {
            enabled: true,
        },
    },
}
```

- Totals are abbreviated, such as `1.2K` or `3.0M`. Use `label.formatter` to change them.
- The column is as wide as its widest label, but no narrower than `minWidth`. Set `width` to fix it instead.

## Customisation

### Width and Placement

In a Financial Chart, set `widthRatio` and `placement` on `volumeProfile` to change the size and side of the bars.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Width and Placement" name="customisation" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    volumeProfile: {
        data: profile,
        upKey: 'upVolume',
        downKey: 'downVolume',
        placement: 'left',
        widthRatio: 0.75,
    },
}
```

In this example:

- `widthRatio` sets the length of the longest bar as a ratio of the series area width. It defaults to `0.5`.
- `placement` sets the edge the bars extend from, `'left'` or `'right'`. It defaults to `'right'`.

### Colours

By default, the bars use the `up` and `down` fills of the [theme palette](themes/#palette).

Set `up` and `down` to style the bars of each direction with options such as `fill`, `fillOpacity`, `stroke` and `strokeWidth`. These take precedence over the theme palette.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Colours" name="bar-colours" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    //...other volume profile options
    up: { fill: '#F2C12E', stroke: '#B8901A' },
    down: { fill: '#2E6BF2', stroke: '#1A45A8' },
}
```

In this example:

- `up` and `down` colour the bars of the up and down volume.
- A `stroke` is 1 pixel wide unless `strokeWidth` is set.

The [status bar](./financial-charts-configuration/#chart-features) uses the `up.fill` and `down.fill` colours to display these values.

